  "contract": "Per-node lifecycle notification must be scoped to the region that was actually committed/published, and membership must be published atomically with a record of the scope it belongs to. Concretely: whenever a system recomputes a set of tree nodes (dependencies, effects, matches, subscribers) and derives \"newly entered\" and \"newly left\" nodes by set difference against the previous set, the difference alone is not authoritative — the code must also know where the delivered/committed region stops, so that nodes belonging to a sub-branch that was superseded (aborted, replaced by a placeholder/fallback, or still unsettled) never have their attach/detach (mount/unmount, subscribe/unsubscribe, ref attach/detach) callbacks run; and the published membership must carry the identity of the branch/epoch it was computed for, and be published through a single batching point so that a listener re-entering the store during notification cannot observe a membership whose extent does not match the region that was actually delivered.",
  "defect_location": {
    "repo": "jotai",
    "summary": "The entered-and-left decision lives in src/vanilla/internals.ts:L929 (BUILDING_BLOCK_mountDependencies) which is reached from the recompute/read path — BUILDING_BLOCK_readAtomState (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L652-L831) and BUILDING_BLOCK_recomputeInvalidatedAtoms (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L560-L649) — and from BUILDING_BLOCK_writeAtomState (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L866-L928). mountDependencies decides which nodes entered and which left purely by differencing the freshly captured dependency set against the previously mounted set, then runs the per-node lifecycle through BUILDING_BLOCK_mountAtom (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L967-L1030, which invokes the atom's onMount via hasOnMount at src/vanilla/internals.ts:L297 and BUILDING_BLOCK_atomOnMount at src/vanilla/internals.ts:L471) and BUILDING_BLOCK_unmountAtom (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L1031-L1070, running the OnUnmount declared at src/vanilla/internals.ts:L17 and src/vanilla/atom.ts:L34-L36). Nothing in that difference carries any notion of whether the computation whose dependency set is being installed is the one whose value was actually delivered: a read that was superseded while its promise was still unsettled is replaced by a stand-in value/promise via BUILDING_BLOCK_setAtomStateValueOrPromise (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L1071-L1100) together with addPendingPromiseToDependency (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L335-L346) and BUILDING_BLOCK_abortPromise / BUILDING_BLOCK_registerAbortHandler (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L1150-L1178), yet the superseded branch's dependency set is still installed and still drives mount/unmount. The membership itself (AtomState.d / Mounted.d, declared at src/vanilla/internals.ts:L29-L68) is written with no record of the branch/epoch (EpochNumber, src/vanilla/internals.ts:L20; StoreEpochHolder, src/vanilla/internals.ts:L199) it was computed for, and it is published while listeners are being run out of BUILDING_BLOCK_flushCallbacks (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L500-L559) and getMountedOrPendingDependents (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L347-L372), so a subscriber registered through BUILDING_BLOCK_storeSub (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L1127-L1149) that re-enters via BUILDING_BLOCK_storeGet (src/vanilla/internals.ts:L1101-L1105) during that flush observes a dependency extent that includes the branch that was never delivered. The React binding is where the stand-in is manufactured and where the never-delivered branch becomes user-visible: createContinuablePromise (src/react/useAtomValue.ts:L60-L119) and useAtomValue (src/react/useAtomValue.ts:L120-L160). The three scoped-notification contracts this must be brought in line with are all graph-verified elsewhere in the folder: react carries the explicit held-back-subtree flag through the commit walk so a hidden subtree runs no attach/detach (packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberCommitWork.js:L3103 safelyDetachRef, :L3301 recursivelyTraverseReappearLayoutEffects, with the effect lists in packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberCommitEffects.js:L141); tldraw's signal layer attaches and detaches only along the branch genuinely depended upon (packages/state/src/lib/EffectScheduler.ts:L134 attach, :L149 detach, :L89-L133 scheduling); and query funnels every observer notification through one batching point (packages/query-core/src/notifyManager.ts:L99). NOTE ON SURFACE COVERAGE: the merged graph I was given spans fourteen repositories, not fifteen — the 'router' checkout is absent from it entirely (probes for matchRoutes, RouterCore, createFileRoute, createBrowserRouter, useNavigate, @tanstack/router-core and @tanstack/history all return no node; '@tanstack/react-router' resolves only to a dependency entry inside db's examples). Every path below was found in the graph and carries a repo/source_file; I have named no path I could not confirm there.",
